          "key": "jefferies",
          "question": "What happened in the Jefferies tube with the phase-doubled conduits?",
          "answer": {
            "answer": "Hinami, as we both experienced in the Jefferies tube: we entered the tight vertical crawlspace together; the conduit bundles were shimmering and doubled in phase, with temporal desynchronization much thicker inside. You pointed out the phase-doubling at the junction as anchor despite fearing erasure. A temporal duplicate of you resolved ahead—identical fox ears and tails but different clothes, flickering with residue. I positioned between you, sonic on the junction. You noted the echoed fragments ('log entry supplemental... phase variance increasing') came from all around, not the figure. On your word I triggered the low resonance pulse; phase variance collapsed, duplicate merged into you, fragments became coherent supplemental log data feeding the systems. Desynchronization flatlined, hollow quality gone, Deck 14 stable. You later reported feeling normal again but with a dragging sensation as if something was taken from you, and that you had felt 'not myself'—which you found uncomfortable. I offered tea to revisit or to drop it. Crew return versus logs only remains open.",
